This project aims to provide mass and balance calculation sheets for
specific aircraft. The intention is that the sheets should be usable
without an internet connection after a sheet has been downloaded to
the local computer (iPad etc.).

The publish page for the sheets is here:

http://kaltsi.github.io/Mass-and-Balance/

If you want to create an m&b sheet for your own plane, take a look at the
existing specification files under the specs subdirectory, then create a new
JSON file there and run the export.sh script. The spec format is documented in
specs/README.md.

The generator is parse_template.py, which renders template.html.j2 with Jinja2:

    ./parse_template.py template.html.j2 specs/oh-kas.json out

export.sh runs it for every spec file. A spec key that is not set falls back to
the default written in the template.

The template variables are the JSON keys (registration, aircraft_type, data_source,
fuel_density_kg_per_l, envelope, invalid_data) plus the load point lists: load_points
(every load point, in spec order) and extra (the load points that are not part of the
fixed calculation chains). Values are formatted for JavaScript with the js filter.

The load point name placeholders (lndw, tow, fuel, ...) resolve to the load point name
when the spec has that row, otherwise to the variable name written in the template
(g_lw, g_tow, ...).

To run it in a container:

    docker build -t mass-and-balance .
    docker run --rm -v "$PWD/out:/app/out" mass-and-balance specs/oh-kas.json out
